# Quick Start

Get started with the SuperInstance ecosystem in 5 minutes.

## Hello World: Privacy-First LLM

This example shows how to redact sensitive data before sending it to an LLM.

### 1. Create a New Project

```bash
cargo new my-ai-app
cd my-ai-app
```

### 2. Add Dependencies

Edit `Cargo.toml`:

```toml
[package]
name = "my-ai-app"
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2021"

[dependencies]
privox = "0.1"
tokio = { version = "1", features = ["full"] }
```

### 3. Write Code

Edit `src/main.rs`:

```rust
use privox::{Redactor, RedactorConfig, TokenVault};

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    // Create vault and redactor
    let vault = TokenVault::in_memory()?;
    let mut redactor = Redactor::new(RedactorConfig::default(), vault);

    // Redact sensitive data
    let text = "Contact john@example.com for API key sk-1234567890";
    let result = redactor.redact(text, "session-1")?;

    println!("Original: {}", text);
    println!("Redacted: {}", result.redacted_text);
    // Output: "Contact [EMAIL_0001] for API key [APIKEY_0001]"

    // In real use: Send redacted.redacted_text to LLM
    // let response = llm.generate(&redacted.redacted_text).await?;

    // Restore original values
    // let final = redactor.reinflate(&response);

    Ok(())
}
```

### 4. Run

```bash
cargo run
```

## Multi-Agent Consensus

Coordinate multiple AI agents with voting:

```rust
use tripartite::{Agent, ConsensusEngine, ConsensusConfig, AgentInput, AgentOutput};
use async_trait::async_trait;

struct MyAgent {
    name: String,
    response: String,
    confidence: f32,
}

#[async_trait]
impl Agent for MyAgent {
    fn name(&self) -> &str { &self.name }
    fn role(&self) -> &str { "Custom agent" }
    fn is_ready(&self) -> bool { true }
    fn model(&self) -> &str { "my-model" }

    async fn process(&self, _input: AgentInput) -> tripartite::Result<AgentOutput> {
        Ok(AgentOutput::new(&self.name, self.response.clone(), self.confidence))
    }
}

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    use std::sync::Arc;

    // Create 3 agents
    let agents = vec![
        Arc::new(MyAgent { name: "Agent1".to_string(), response: "42".to_string(), confidence: 0.90 }),
        Arc::new(MyAgent { name: "Agent2".to_string(), response: "42".to_string(), confidence: 0.85 }),
        Arc::new(MyAgent { name: "Agent3".to_string(), response: "42".to_string(), confidence: 0.88 }),
    ];

    // Run consensus
    let engine = ConsensusEngine::new(ConsensusConfig::default(), agents);
    let outcome = engine.run("What is the meaning of life?").await?;

    println!("Consensus: {}", outcome.is_consensus());
    println!("Content: {}", outcome.content);

    Ok(())
}
```

## Vector Search (RAG)

Build a semantic search engine:

```rust
use knowledge_vault::{KnowledgeVault, LocalEmbedder, DocumentIndexer};

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    // Open vault
    let vault = KnowledgeVault::open("knowledge.db", 384)?;
    let embedder = LocalEmbedder::new(384)?;

    // Index documents
    let indexer = DocumentIndexer::new(vault.clone(), embedder);
    indexer.index_file("README.md").await?;

    // Search semantically
    let query_emb = embedder.embed("How do I search documents?").await?;
    let results = vault.search(&query_emb, 5)?;

    for result in results {
        println!("Score: {:.2} | {}", result.score, result.content);
    }

    Ok(())
}
```

